1	# OrcaSlicer dialogs during tool calls, 2026-11-03
2	
3	Approved by Kenneth on 2026-11-03 ("ok. tell the main session to execute on this plan"). This replaces the earlier cause-tracking design.
4	
5	## Rule
6	
7	A dialog that opens while a JusPrin tool call runs is answered with the least change, and the call's result says what it asked and how it was answered. Every other dialog shows, as OrcaSlicer shows it. Nothing carries past the end of a call.
8	
9	## Mechanism
10	
11	- One `wxModalDialogHook`, registered once. Its `Enter` calls today's `dispatch_dialog` (`Workspace/DialogListeners.cpp`): an answer is returned, otherwise `wxID_NONE` and the dialog shows. wxWidgets calls the hook from every `wxDialog::ShowModal` and from native message boxes and file dialogs.
12	- The fork's `answer_modal` call and declaration leave `GUI_Utils.hpp`; `DPIAware::ShowModal` is upstream again.
13	- All existing listener sites stay as they are, including the person's-own-open listener (`OrcaWorkspaceAdapter::file_open_started`, `m_open_answers`), which runs outside any tool call.
14	- The tool-call rule is one more least-change listener, opened once per call by the coordinator around `execute()`. It is outermost, so a tool's own listener answers first. Order and "one listener answers" come from `dispatch_dialog`'s innermost-to-outermost walk.
15	- Tests observe dialogs through one observer the app's hook calls when nothing answered and the dialog is about to show. A test's own `wxModalDialogHook` would be newer than the app's and so called first, seeing dialogs before the listeners.
16	
17	## Not covered, on purpose
18	
19	- A dialog that opens after a call ends shows: the slice error box after `slice_start`, an arrange error, "Incorrect password" from the connection callback.
20	- Non-modal windows (`Show()` without `ShowModal`) are not touched.
21	- "Incorrect password": a separate one-line exception in `GUI_App.cpp` (skip `show_dialog` while the printer chat waits for that device) was proposed and is **not approved yet**.
22	
23	## Risks to check
24	
25	- Native Mac message boxes have no wx children: `read_dialog` sees the title only, and the listener falls back to Cancel, marked unrecognized.
26	- A tool call that lets the event loop run might let a person's click raise a dialog inside the call's scope. Untested.
27	
28	## Test plan
29	
30	1. Map each listener site to a check that drives a real dialog through it; add one where a site has none. Prove each is real by disabling the listeners and watching it fail.
31	2. Move the test probes (`real_adapter_harness` `DialogProbe` / `ShownDialogs`, `tests/shell/dialog_witness.hpp`) to the observer. Same results on today's seam.
32	3. Switch the seam. Rerun the workspace harness and the shell harness (default, `--print-issues`, `--printer-setup`, `--dialog-routing`).
33	4. Log every dialog the hook answers that `DPIAware::ShowModal` never passed (plain `wxDialog`, native boxes, file pickers) and review each.
